# 6. GLOBAL SPACING, ALIGNMENT AND GRID SYSTEM

One of the biggest problems is inconsistent alignment.

Establish a reusable layout and spacing system.

Create a consistent spacing scale rather than using arbitrary spacing values throughout the application.

Review:

- Page padding.
- Content width.
- Section spacing.
- Heading margins.
- Paragraph spacing.
- Form spacing.
- Button spacing.
- Navigation spacing.
- Sidebar spacing.
- Card spacing.
- Toolbar spacing.
- Footer spacing.

## Container system

Establish appropriate container sizes for different content types.

For example:

- Narrow containers for reading and lesson content.
- Medium containers for forms and focused tasks.
- Wide containers for dashboards and technology catalogues.
- Flexible full-width containers for code editors and professional workspaces.

Do not force all pages into the same maximum width.

## Alignment rules

Ensure:

- Page headings align with their content.
- Buttons align naturally with headings and controls.
- Forms use consistent label alignment.
- Tables align correctly.
- Navigation items are vertically aligned.
- Icons align with their accompanying text.
- Content follows a consistent vertical rhythm.
- Page headers do not have awkward spacing.
- Components do not randomly shift between pages.
- Sections have consistent left and right boundaries.

Use proper CSS Grid and Flexbox layouts.

Avoid unnecessary absolute positioning and arbitrary pixel offsets.

